<p>A humanoid robot completed a half marathon in Beijing in 50 minutes and 26 seconds, a time multiple outlets said was faster than the human world record for the distance. Coverage cast the finish as a milestone in humanoid locomotion and a high-profile demonstration of China’s progress in embodied robotics.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/xeUkUS9FQOwPUZ8r5stFz_jCBrPhNPkVBD6V--A4O9SLZO4rysa-DfTat12a53Lb68Fk7ajFhClLmtpwMYpYbIoDd83-bSHycIGTu8Fart4f9cAE3rg-L5HWEk7J8QI6Vux_Beqy5i_tk194eMUEuCiu8Fg26hxQRf9CmTe0d8Bf7UV_k1Q' alt='The 5-foot-5 humanoid robot Lightning, with its approximately 3-foot-long legs striding, showed its form in a half-marathon race on Sunday in Beijing.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Large field: Organizers brought together more than 300 robots from over 100 teams, turning the Beijing event into a broad industry showcase rather than a one-off demonstration.</li><li>Honor link: NPR identified the winning entry as coming from Honor, best known as a Chinese smartphone maker, showing how newer and less traditional players are moving into robotics.</li><li>Global participation: PBS reported that international teams took part, so the competition was more than a domestic Chinese showcase.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>PBS NewsHour: The outlet framed the race as part of a broader technology contest with the United States, using the event to show how China wants to display visible progress in humanoid robotics. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/humanoid-robot-wins-beijing-half-marathon-defeating-the-human-world-record'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Semafor: It described the finish as evidence of rapid gains in China’s physical AI sector, where software advances still have to translate into steady movement in the real world. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/19/2026/chinas-robot-half-marathon-shows-off-humanoid-advances'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>New York Times: The paper treated the result as a technological milestone reached in a public half-marathon, giving robot progress a vivid benchmark general audiences could easily grasp. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/19/world/asia/running-robot-sets-record.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/20/g-s1-118086/humanoid-robot-half-marathon'>A humanoid robot sprints past the human half-marathon world record in Beijing race</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/19/2026/chinas-robot-half-marathon-shows-off-humanoid-advances'>China&#x27;s robot half marathon shows off humanoid advances</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/humanoid-robot-wins-beijing-half-marathon-defeating-the-human-world-record'>Humanoid robot wins Beijing half-marathon, defeating the human world record</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/19/world/asia/running-robot-sets-record.html'>A Humanoid Robot Races to a Record Half-Marathon Finish</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/humanoid-robot-sprints-victory-beijing-beating-human-half-132179294'>Humanoid robot sprints to victory in Beijing, beating human half-marathon record</a> - abcnews.com</li></ul>